# SPA fallback for BrowserRouter. Any path under packages/<pkg>/dist/ whose last
# segment has no file extension is served that package's index.html, so React
# Router can take over on a deep link or a page refresh.
#
# The extension test is a negative lookahead in the rule pattern rather than a
# RewriteCond on %{REQUEST_PATH}. In a context level valve neither
# %{REQUEST_PATH} nor %{REQUEST_FILENAME} expands to the request path, so a
# condition on them passes for every request and asset URLs get answered with
# index.html. The rule pattern is matched against the context relative URL, which
# is the value the valve actually rewrites.
#
# Matching on "no extension" is a whitelist, not a list of asset extensions to
# keep in sync: everything the build emits has one, so assets are served normally
# and a missing asset still returns a clean 404 rather than a page of HTML.
# index.html has an extension too, so the rewrite cannot loop.
RewriteRule ^(/packages/[^/]+/dist/)(?!.*\.[A-Za-z0-9]+$).*$ $1index.html [L]
